---
import Section from '../Section.astro';
import Container from '../Container.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../SectionHeader.astro';
import Button from '../Button.astro';

/*
  Pitch page section 6 — see it working (docs/pitch-demo-sitemap.md §4.6).

  The hand-off: the one thing this build can do that a deck cannot. One framing
  sentence, one entry point, no menu of deep links — a choice of four doors turns
  a ninety-second walkthrough into a decision nobody makes.

  The link is a plain anchor, same tab: a new tab breaks the back path and
  orphans the ask, which is the section this walk has to return to.

  DESTINATION IS A STAND-IN. The real target is /demo, the product walkthrough
  subtree, which is a separate build and does not exist yet. Rather than ship a
  dead link at the one lateral action on the page, it points at /events — the
  closest thing currently in the repo to "a room you can actually open." Change
  this href to "/demo" when that subtree lands; nothing else in this file needs
  to move.

  The id is load-bearing: the demo bar the sitemap specifies returns to
  /#see-it-working so the scroll resumes here rather than at the top of the page.

  COPY STATUS: the framing sentence is a plain statement of fact about what the
  demo is — the honesty this section exists to carry, not an invented claim —
  pending `copywriter`'s pass. The heading is the brief's own section name.
*/
---

<Section id="see-it-working">
  <Container>
    <SectionHeader kicker="The proof" heading="See it working." />

    <p class="framing">
      This is a working demonstration, not a screenshot. The gatherings and cities in it are
      examples, and nothing you tap signs you up for anything.
    </p>

    <Button href="/events" variant="primary" size="lg">Enter the demo</Button>
  </Container>
</Section>

<style>
  .framing {
    color: var(--color-text-body);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    max-width: 46ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
  }
</style>
